## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical secure file upload handling, a common real-world area accessible to beginners. It demonstrates concrete mitigation steps rather than theoretical knowledge.

## Key Concepts

- File-type validation using magic bytes
- Size limits and safe storage
- Safe filename handling and path traversal protection
- Non-executable upload directory and proper permissions
- Basic CI checks for upload validation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Implementation sketch for safe image upload checks
function isSafeImage(file) {
  const sizeLimit = 1024 * 1024;
  if (file.size > sizeLimit) return false;
  const header = new Uint8Array(file.slice(0, 4));
  const magic = (header[0] << 24) | (header[1] << 16) | (header[2] << 8) | header[3];
  const isPng = magic === 0x89504E47;
  const isJpeg = magic === 0xFFD8FFE0;
  if (!(isPng || isJpeg)) return false;
  const mime = file.type;
  if (mime !== 'image/png' && mime !== 'image/jpeg') return false;
  return true;
}
```

